{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The World of Entertainment"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Directing a Movie"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 17}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le17ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "  Talking About the Past: The Present Perfect Tense vs. The Simple Past Tense and Used to and Would"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. <br/> You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past tense</span> to talk about many kinds of past events: short, quickly finished actions, longer situations and repeated events. <br/> You use <span class=\"strong\">used to </span> and<span class=\"strong\">would </span> to talk about past habits which are now finished. There is an idea that circumstances have changed. You do not use it to talk about what happened at a past time. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense </span> to talk about experience.<br/> When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span>, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">have learned </span> English. </span> = I learned English in the past and now I can speak English.. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Usually, when you use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past tense</span>, the time of the finished action is clear from the context or explicitly mentioned in the sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Yesterday</span> , I <span class=\"strong\">went </span> to the store.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is clear when the action occurred. In this sentence we would not use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>. (<span class=\"italic\"><strike>Yesterday, I have been to the store</strike></span>)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Both <span class=\"strong\">used to </span> and <span class=\"strong\">would </span> talk about past habits which no longer exist, but there are a couple of things to note about the usage of these expressions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "1. <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> cannot be used to talk about past states. You must use used to.</span> <br>For example: <span class=\"italic\">I used to have a dog.</span> <span class=\"italic\"><strike>I would have a dog. </strike> </span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "2. You use <span class=\"strong\">used to </span> to talk about regular, important habitual behavior. <br> For example: <span class=\"italic\">I used to smoke. <strike>I would smoke.</strike> </span> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I used to do too much. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Then I started to let everyone do what they came to do. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have never looked back."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I was very confident, and saw every problem as"}, {"type": "example", "content": "This was the most important lesson I learned on my first film. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "That knowledge has helped me ever since. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We have had some really complicated sets this time around."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use an active structure when you want the \u2018doer' of the action to be the subject.<br/> You use a passive structure when you want the \u2018receiver' of the action to be the subject. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the </span> Present Continuous </span> to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Any director who a strong production team<span class=\"strong\"> is supporting </span> should realize that they are beyond lucky.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the </span> Present Perfect </span> to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">People on set<span class=\"strong\"> have left </span> the actors to me. </span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often choose the <span class=\"strong\">passive form </span> when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents </span> (the doers) are common in writing. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present <br/> Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"am/are/is + being + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Any director who <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is being supported </span> by a strong production team should realize that they are beyond lucky. </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" have/has + been + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Today on set the actors <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been left </span> to me.</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When they are being recognized, they are happy and appreciative."}, {"type": "example", "content": "While this, my new movie, is being made, my team has been thanked daily."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they have ever been helped as many other highly creative people as I have, they should acknowledge that their jobs have been made far easier. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Today on set the actors have been left to me."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to support"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200bgive \u200bhelp and encouragement to someone or something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Any director who is being supported by a strong production team should realize that they are beyond lucky. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about a film."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "production team"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the group of technical staff who produce a play, a television show, a recording, or a film"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Any director who is being supported by a strong production team is fortunate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "beyond lucky"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "extremely fortunate"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That team is beyond lucky. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to acknowledge"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200baccept, \u200badmit, or \u200brecognize the \u200btruth of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They should acknowledge that their jobs have been made far easier."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "appreciative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "being \u200bgrateful for something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  When they are being recognized, they are happy and appreciative."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to overcome"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200b\u200bsucceed in \u200bdealing with a something difficult"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was very confident, and saw every problem as a challenge to be overcome."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "audition"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to try out for a role in a play or film"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would hold auditions that included both cold readings and improvisations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "I've never looked back"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move forward with confidence and without regrets"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I have never looked back."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob07aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rushes"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the raw, unedited footage shot during the making of a movie"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We've watched the rushes daily."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob07aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to the library and look up jobs related to film production."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make notes on two different jobs that interest you."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the notes to write a short summary of the job responsibilities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain why you might enjoy doing that job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your paragraphs to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find out about  jobs related to film production."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use my notes to write about two different jobs that interest me."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my written work with a partner and discuss it."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about film and work."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about habits in the past."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "cont